--EXPECT--
```nvs
Core\Json::encode(mixed $value, { pretty?: bool, escapeUnicode?: bool } $options): string
```

Converts `$value` to JSON text. It can be a scalar, an array, an anonymous object or an instance of a class with `#[Json\Derive]`. The text is on one line unless `pretty` is set.

**Parameters**

- `$value` — The value to encode: `null`, `bool`, `int`, `uint`, `float`, `decimal`, `string`, an array, a `{ name: value }` shape, or an instance of a class with `#[Json\Derive]`.
- `pretty` — Writes the output across several lines, with indentation. By default, the output is on one line.
- `escapeUnicode` — Writes every non-ASCII character as a `\uXXXX` escape. By default, UTF-8 text is written as it is.

**Returns** The JSON text. It is a `tainted string` when `$value` can contain text from outside the program. That is a `tainted` string, or a `mixed` or `object` value, anywhere inside it.

**Throws**

- `LogicError` — `$value` contains something that JSON cannot represent. This is a `NaN` or infinite `float`, a value of a type with no JSON form, an instance of a class without `#[Json\Derive]`, or more than 1024 levels of nesting.
